From 0c71df425af5b16abf830937ff6c72f978c517b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:17:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: q8_1 residual and scale-f16 rounding use the ds
 store's own f16 conversion; arifi-op-probe op-level int8 tools

lane-296 int8 goal maker. packHalf2x16 rounds toward zero on RDNA3 (AMD proprietary driver) while the f16vec2 ds store rounds to nearest, so the two-digit residual was taken against a different d1 than the kernel applies: floor 5.1e-4 relative on real ssm_out inputs. With one conversion the GPU equals the ideal host simulator: 1.38e-4 (L0), 3e-5 (L16/L32). Affects only GGML_ARIFI_Q8_0_CM1_2D and GGML_ARIFI_Q8_1_SCALE (default off). tools/arifi-op-probe: arifi-op-probe (synth, replay, multi: one Q8_0 matmul on Vulkan vs an f64 host reference, with q8_1 simulators) and arifi-op-capture (dumps a real forward pass's matmul inputs and outputs).

Lane: lane-296
